// Original bilingual V41 campaign and specialist copy.
    {TEXT("铁路分遣队配属"),TEXT("RAIL DETACHMENT")},
    {TEXT("夺取中央与第一道敌壕，或迫使敌军撤退"),TEXT("Capture the centre and first enemy trench, or force a retreat")},
    {TEXT("冬季巡逻只配属轻装分队与烟幕，不接通重炮、机队和装甲。"),TEXT("This winter patrol takes light sections and smoke. Heavy batteries, aircraft and armour are not attached.")},
    {TEXT("居民区邻段不批准毒气与空中轰炸。"),TEXT("Gas and aerial bombing are not authorised beside inhabited streets.")},
    {TEXT("夺下中央补给湾后，携弹队可缩短下一轮整备。"),TEXT("Taking the central supply bay brings carriers forward and eases the next preparation.")},
    {TEXT("中央支点易手后，敌军预备队会沿原通路组织反击。"),TEXT("After the central post changes hands, enemy reserves will counterattack along their approach.")},
    {TEXT("中央支点已夺取。留一队掩护，敌军预备队正在接近。"),TEXT("Central post secured. Leave a section covering it; enemy reserves are approaching.")},
    {TEXT("中央补给湾接通。携弹队正在为下一轮出击整备。"),TEXT("The central supply bay is open. Carriers are preparing the next advance.")},
    {TEXT("本连的通路已经接通，接替部队可以通过。"),TEXT("The company route is open for the following troops.")},
    {TEXT("敌军切断了本连最后的交通线。"),TEXT("The enemy has severed the company approach.")},
    {TEXT("把重枪稳在泥上"),TEXT("Steady the heavy rifle")},
    {TEXT("枪口前的二十三号"),TEXT("No. 23 at the muzzle")},
    {TEXT("Tankgewehr 需要专门的支撑与瞄准训练。射手把沉重枪身稳住，携弹手照看侧面；把瞄准点留在装甲的薄弱处，命中仍不等于必然击穿。"),TEXT("The Tankgewehr demands its own support and aiming drill. The gunner steadies the heavy rifle while his carrier watches the flank. Better aim finds vulnerable armour; a hit still does not guarantee penetration.")},
    {TEXT("No.23 枪榴弹把投掷延伸到壕口之外。练习专用发射弹、枪口支架与安全抛射，让散布收拢在观察到的枪位附近；步枪掩护仍不可少。"),TEXT("The No. 23 carries a grenade beyond a hand throw. Drill with launching cartridges, the retaining bracket and safe elevation gathers the shots around an observed post. Rifle cover remains essential.")},
    {TEXT("专门分队"),TEXT("Specialist sections")},
    {TEXT("留一人照看枪身"),TEXT("A man beside the rifle")},
    {TEXT("携弹手的肩带"),TEXT("The carrier's shoulder strap")},
    {TEXT("大口径枪弹逐发交到射手手中。携弹手活着并留在小队时，重新装填更从容；失去同伴以后，射手只能独自承担整套工作。"),TEXT("The heavy cartridges pass to the gunner one at a time. A living carrier beside his section eases each reload. Without that companion, the gunner must manage the whole task alone.")},
    {TEXT("枪榴弹与专用发射弹分开携行，携弹手在发射间隙把下一发送到射手身边。有同伴伴随，装填便更顺畅；孤身射手没有这份照应。"),TEXT("Grenades and launching cartridges travel separately. Between shots the carrier brings the next round to the gunner. Reloading is smoother with his companion nearby; a lone gunner loses that help.")},
    {TEXT("携弹联络"),TEXT("Ammunition carriers")},
    {TEXT("接通前沿的铜线"),TEXT("Copper wire to the forward post")},
    {TEXT("把电话送进新壕"),TEXT("Carry the telephone forward")},
    {TEXT("电话线随夺壕向前延伸。让一队驻守中央之后的第一道敌壕，观察员便能缩短间接火力的第一轮传令；空壕与断开的前沿没有这项便利。"),TEXT("Lay the telephone wire into captured ground. A section holding the first enemy trench beyond the centre shortens the first indirect-fire request. An empty post cannot maintain that connection.")},
    {TEXT("前沿电话"),TEXT("Forward telephone")},
    {TEXT("以枪榴弹压住近处枪位，射手需要稳定支撑与携弹手掩护。"),TEXT("Use rifle grenades against nearby weapon posts. The gunner needs steady support and his carrier beside him.")},
    {TEXT("支撑重型反坦克枪逐发射击装甲；装填缓慢，需要步兵掩护侧面。"),TEXT("Support the heavy anti-tank rifle for single shots against armour. Reloading is slow; infantry must guard its flanks.")},
    {TEXT("费迪南德·冯·夸斯特"),TEXT("Ferdinand von Quast")},
    {TEXT("1850年出生的步兵将领，先后指挥第九军与近卫军，1917年秋接掌第六集团军。利斯河攻势中，他的部队向河沟与道路间的薄弱地段推进；眼前的快速突入仍需要后续步兵与补给接上。"),TEXT("Born in 1850, Quast commanded IX Corps and the Guard Corps before taking Sixth Army in autumn 1917. During the Lys offensive his troops pressed through weak sectors among streams and roads. Rapid gains still needed following infantry and supplies.")},
    {TEXT("SMLE 以专用发射弹抛射 No.23 枪榴弹。射手稳住支架，携弹手供应弹药；逐发装填，适合打击固定枪位。"),TEXT("The SMLE launches a No.23 grenade with a special cartridge. The gunner steadies the support while a bearer supplies rounds. Single-shot loading suits attacks on fixed gun posts."),TEXT("No.23 枪榴弹由装有发射杆和支架的 SMLE 抛射。射手需要稳定支撑与专用发射弹，携弹手在身旁照应；它不能像步枪一样连续开火。")},
    {TEXT("枪榴弹从掩护后打击近处枪位，步枪与投弹班随后接近。友军需避开弹着区。"),TEXT("Rifle grenades strike nearby posts from cover as rifles and bombers approach. Keep friendly troops clear of the impact area."),TEXT("从掩护后压住近处枪位，再让步枪与投弹班接近。不要把枪榴弹送进自己人的壕口。")},
    {TEXT("Tankgewehr M1918 架稳后逐发射击装甲。装填缓慢，命中仍可能未击穿；携弹手在旁掩护。"),TEXT("The Tankgewehr M1918 fires single rounds from a supported position. Loading is slow and a hit can fail to penetrate. The bearer guards the gunner."),TEXT("Tankgewehr M1918 以单发大口径弹对付装甲。沉重枪身必须得到支撑，装填缓慢，命中也不等于必然击穿；携弹手留在身边保护射手。")},
    {TEXT("反坦克枪组守住装甲接近线，普通步兵保护侧翼。两人枪组难以抵挡近距离步兵攻击。"),TEXT("Tank-rifle teams cover the armour approaches while ordinary infantry protect their flanks. The two-man crew is vulnerable to close infantry attacks."),TEXT("让反坦克枪组看住装甲接近线，以普通步兵保护侧面。保持距离与稳定阵位，别让它独自应付冲来的步兵。")},
